{"id":"8b35a353043b495ece2d92d263bde320304aafeb7a1ba4b39a7414d78d0813a2","pubkey":"e58143f793e4bf805a4df6cdc0289e352b3cf08a7b3e6afaaf89dd497bf0f4a6","created_at":1782664535,"content":"EU governments lost the fight over mass surveillance of private chats and now they want a rematch on their own terms.\n\nAmbassadors pushed Friday to revive temporary scanning of WhatsApp, Messenger, and more for \"CSAM.\" \n\nThis is after Parliament voted it down 311 against in March and the legal basis already expired.\n\nThe Council wants to override Parliament and scan 450 million people's messages, treating everyone as suspects. Error rates hit 13-50%. \n\nThis clears the path for next week's big \"Chat Control\" push into end-to-end encryption.\n\nhttps://reclaimthenet.org/brussels-could-reopen-the-fight-to-scan-your-private-chats","tags":[["r","wss://sendit.nosflare.com/"],["r","wss://wot.utxo.one/"],["r","wss://nostrelites.org/"],["r","wss://wot.nostr.party/"],["client","Primal Web"]]}
